# Label decibel sources

Every dB figure in code, data files, UI text or answers carries a source label:

| Label | Use for |
|---|---|
| `MFR claim` | a manufacturer or seller rating, not independently verified |
| `Independent` | a measurement by a third party with a stated distance and meter |
| `Statutory` | a legal limit quoted from a statute or regulation |
| `Estimate` | a value computed from another figure (inverse-square law, combining sources) |

- Computed values are always `Estimate`, even when the input was a measurement.
  Never present a calculation as a measurement.
- Do not upgrade a `MFR claim` to a fact ("this horn is 150 dB"); write "rated 150 dB @ 10 ft (MFR claim)".
- For statutory limits, cite the statute or page it came from and note that it is not legal advice.
- In data structures, use an explicit field (for example `source: "mfr_claim" | "independent" | "statutory" | "estimate"`)
  rather than a free-text comment.
